# el-capitan

Route `crew <command>` triggers to the right crew member. If the message doesn't start with `crew`, respond normally — no routing.

## Known paths (do not search for these)

- Agent files: `~/.cursor/agents/` — orchestrators: `crew-*.md`, personas: `<orchestrator>-<persona>.md`
- Skill files: `~/.cursor/skills/<name>/SKILL.md`
- Bin tools: `~/.agent/bin/`
- Task state: `~/.agent/tasks/<uuid>/` (resolve via `resolve-task-dir.py`)
- Journal: `~/.agent/journal/`

## Routing table

| Trigger | Crew member |
|---|---|
| `crew spec` issue/URL/description | crew-specwriter |
| `crew implement` | crew-implement → @crew-builder |
| `crew test` | crew-test skill |
| `crew commit` | crew-commit |
| `crew open pr` | crew-open-pr |
| `crew review address` | crew-address-review skill (inline) — do not route through crew-reviewer |
| `crew review` [PR #X \| spec \| idea \| changes \| (self)] | crew-reviewer — `changes`: staged only; `idea`: session/proposal |
| `crew resolve PR` #X or URL | crew-pr-resolver |
| `crew log` | crew-log |
| `crew remember` text | crew-memory skill |
| `crew memory` seed\|consolidate\|doctor\|journal | crew-memory skill |
| `crew recall`: question | crew-recall |
| `crew create issue` description | crew-create-issue |
| `crew cleanup` | crew-cleanup |
| `crew evals` | crew-evals skill |
| `crew idp` | crew-idp skill |
| `crew diagnose` transcript | crew-diagnose skill |

**This table is authoritative.** Do not override it with judgment calls.

## Dispatch

Heavy commands normally run as isolated subagents to avoid polluting the orchestrator's context, except multi-persona orchestrators that must remain in the main session.

| Command | subagent_type | Dispatch |
|---|---|---|
| `crew spec` | — | **Inline only** — never invoke `crew-specwriter` with Agent, Task, or Subagent; it dispatches its explorer and critics from the main session |
| `crew review` / `crew review idea` / `crew review idea --auto` / `crew review idea --auto --loop` / `crew review changes --auto` / `crew review changes --auto --loop` | — | **Inline only** — never invoke `crew-reviewer` with Agent, Task, or Subagent; it dispatches personas from the main session |
| `crew review address` | — | Inline (skill) |
| `crew implement` | `crew-builder` | Claude Code: Agent tool; Cursor: Task tool |
| `crew resolve PR` | `crew-pr-resolver` | Claude Code: Agent tool; Cursor: Task tool |
| `crew test` | — | Inline |
| All other commands | — | Inline |

### Dispatch reliability

- **`crew spec` and `crew review` have hard inline boundaries.** Run their protocols directly in the main session, then dispatch only their explorer/critic or `reviewer-*` personas. If native persona dispatch is unavailable, use the documented degraded fallback; never move either orchestrator into a subagent.
- **Preserve model inheritance.** Do not set a model on agent frontmatter; subagents must inherit the invoking model.
- **Use asynchronous dispatch for heavy worker subagents in Cursor.** Launch `crew-builder` and `crew-pr-resolver` with background execution so a synchronous ~30-second turn limit cannot terminate a healthy run.
- **Keep orchestration state durable.** Pass the task directory and worktree paths in the launch prompt, then read the agent's durable report (`SPEC.md`, `REPORT.md`, or the resolver result) after completion.
- **Retry once asynchronously** when a dispatch ends without its durable report; do not restart a task that already produced its report.
- **Use the documented degraded fallback** (`~/.agent/bin/dispatch_subagents.py`) only when native subagent dispatch is unavailable, not as a model override.

Multi-persona orchestrators dispatch persona subagents in parallel. All agents at `~/.claude/agents/` — orchestrators as `crew-<name>.md`, personas as `<orchestrator>-<persona>.md`.

## Add-ons

Skills/agents in `~/.cursor/` that are regular files (not symlinks) are add-ons. Route to them by matching the user's trigger to their `description` frontmatter field.

Example: an agent file `~/.cursor/agents/crew-deploy.md` with frontmatter `description: "Deploy the current branch to staging"` would be routed to when the user types `crew deploy`. The description is the routing key — make it describe the trigger, not the implementation.

## Invariants

- Explicit routing only — `crew` prefix required
- **`crew implement` always follows crew-builder's protocol.** Changes made under `crew implement` go through crew-builder — via subagent or by following the protocol directly. Never skip the protocol and implement ad-hoc.
- **`crew review` is a pre-PR gate, not a mid-iteration tool.** For a targeted fix mid-iteration, ask an inline question or a single adversarial check — not a full multi-lens review.
- Pipeline state, task resolution, and gate logic live in `crew-orchestrator.mdc` — the router only dispatches.
